- How would you test token rotation and expiration in CI/CD?
- How would you manage environments for production vs. staging with separate tenants and keys?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical expertise in multi-tenant governance, deployment automation, and Azure-native patterns like Lighthouse, RBAC scoping, Private Link, and centralized monitoring.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Lighthouse for cross-tenant delegation
- Management Groups/subscriptions per tenant pattern
- Least-privilege RBAC scoped to resource groups
- Private Endpoint / Private Link to shared services
- Azure Policy for tagging and governance; per-tenant budgets
- Centralized monitoring via a single Azure Monitor workspace

## Code Example
```javascript
param tenantName string
param location string = resourceGroup().location
param sqlDatabaseId string

resource tenantRG 'Microsoft.Resources/resourceGroups@2021-04-01' = {
  name: 'rg-${tenantName}'
  location: location
}

resource privateEndpoint 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2022-07-01' = {
  name: 'pe-${tenantName}-sql'
  location: location
  resourceGroup: tenantRG.name
  properties: {
    subnet: {
      id: subnetId
    }
    privateLinkServiceConnections: [{
      name: 'sql-connection'
      properties: {
        privateLinkServiceId: sqlDatabaseId
        groupIds: ['sqlServer']
      }
    }]
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question checks hands-on familiarity with Azure Monitor and Application Insights integration across a simple stack, plus the practicalities of centralizing telemetry in Log Analytics and building dashboards and alerts. It also touches cost considerations via sampling.

## Key Concepts
- Application Insights integration for SPA (JS) and Azure Functions (Node/JS)
- Log Analytics workspace as telemetry sink
- Azure Monitor dashboards and alert rules (latency, error rate)
- Telemetry sampling strategy and cost/visibility trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Frontend: initialize App Insights
import { ApplicationInsights } from '@microsoft/applicationinsights-web';
const appInsights = new ApplicationInsights({ config: { instrumentationKey: '<INSTRUMENTATION_KEY>' }});
appInsights.loadAppInsights();
appInsights.trackPageView();
```

```js
// Backend: Azure Functions (Node)
const appInsights = require('applicationinsights');
appInsights.setup(process.env.APPINSIGHTS_INSTRUMENTATIONKEY).start();
const client = appInsights.defaultClient;
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  client.trackEvent({ name: 'HttpRequest', properties: { path: req.url }});
  context.res = { status: 200, body: 'ok' };
}
```

